<> Functional Testing 

> Field Display
=> Checking each field displayed as per design

> Business Logic
=> Check each condition working correctly with valid inputs-positive Test , invalid inputs - Negative Test.

> End to End Flow Testing
-> End to End flow Testing means Checking entire flow of the application from beginning to ending.

> End to End flow Testing two types 
1. End to End flow Happy Path
2. End to End flow Non-Happy Path

> End to End flow Happy Path : Checking Shortest Path with Mandatory fields.
EX1: Gmail : 
step 1 : Login to Gmail
step 2 : create new email - To option
step 3 : No need add CC , BCC , Attachment
step 4 : Click on Send Button

Expected Result : Mail must Send Successfully

> End to End flow Non-Happy Path : checking longest path with mandatory and optional fields.

Ex1: Gmail : 
step 1 : Login to Gmail
step 2 : Create new email - To Option
step 3 : create new email with CCC,BCC,Attachment
step 4 : click on send button

Expected Result : Mail Must send successfully.

How to do Functional Testing of Web Application Via Front-End ?

1. Field Display : Test each field displayed.
2. Business logic Positive : Test with valid Inputs.
3. Business logic Negative : Test with In valid Inputs.
4. End to End flow Happy Path : Test Shortest Path.
5. End to End flow Non-Happy Path : Test Longest Path.


How to do Non-Functional Testing of web application via front-end ?

1. Usability Testing.
2. computability testing.
3. Performance Testing.
4. Security Testing.
5. Localization Testing.


